{"from": "text:irenaeus-haer-3-10-6", "type": "related_to", "to": "passage:mk-16-19", "note": "Reception: Irenaeus, who knows the Gospels, explicitly cites Mark 16:19 in Against Heresies 3.10.6 (c. 184 CE) - over a century older than the earliest manuscript of Mark 16, per the fetched article. Reception of a Gospel text is linked related_to, never attests (calibration). The ending's absence from Sinaiticus and Vaticanus is recorded in the passage variants and in the absent preserves edges."}
{"from": "claim:mk-16-01-08-spices-tomb", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-28-01-mary-tomb", "note": "Mark has three women (Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James, Salome) buying spices to anoint the body and arriving at sunrise; Matthew has two women at dawn and no spices. Mark's messenger is a young man inside the tomb; Matthew's angel descends amid an earthquake and sits on the stone. Mark ends at v8 with the women fleeing in silence; Matthew continues with a joyful report, a guard scene and appearances."}
{"from": "claim:mk-16-01-08-spices-tomb", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-28-02-06-tomb-stone", "note": "Both report the great stone rolled back/away from the tomb's door; Matthew alone supplies the earthquake and the descending angel who rolls it. A Gospel difference, recorded with related_to per calibration."}
{"from": "claim:mk-16-09-14-appearances", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-28-09-17-appearances", "note": "Different appearance traditions: Mark's longer ending has Mary Magdalene, two on the road into the country, and the eleven at table, with disbelieving hearers; Matthew has the women on the way and the eleven on a Galilee mountain."}
{"from": "claim:mk-16-15-18-commission-signs", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-28-19-baptismal-formula", "note": "Both commissions send the disciples out; Mark's has 'he who believes and is baptized will be saved' without Matthew's triune baptismal formula, and adds the signs (new languages, serpents, deadly drink, healing)."}
{"from": "text:irenaeus-haer-3-10-6", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-mark-16-irenaeus"}
