{"from": "text:josephus-war-1-673-spices", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-16-01-08-spices-tomb", "grade": "C", "note": "Herod's 4 BCE funeral: 'five hundred of his domestic servants and freed-men followed, with sweet spices in their hands' - burial spices carried in a first-century Judean funeral procession, the custom of honoring the dead with spices that Mark's spice-buying presupposes; it does not attest the women's purchase itself, so C."}
